Revision history for Ham-CW

0.001  2026-10-24
    - Complete per-method POD and standalone examples; clarify installation,
      data types, timing, file ownership, errors and reception diagnostics.
    - Initial development release for Morse text, timing, PCM WAV and MIDI.
    - International symbols, operational prosigns and Farnsworth generation.
    - Collecting, streaming and path-based APIs with bounded resource use,
      structured errors and immutable decoding snapshots.
    - Experimental audio reception with tone and speed estimation, partial
      text recovery and warnings for ambiguous timing or spacing.
    - Robust envelope seeding for sparse messages and isolated 5 ms impulses.
    - Catchable broken-pipe errors, direct sampled-event MIDI tick rounding,
      canonical decoder segment limits and validated result/error payloads.
    - Optional PDL acceleration, selected explicitly or through auto fallback;
      the default Perl backend uses only core dependencies.
    - Explicit overwrite for WAV and MIDI file output; failed replacements
      preserve existing files.
    - Independent signal fixtures, reception matrix, backend comparisons and
      regression tests. Benchmark tooling reports local workload measurements.
    - Correct automatic speed estimates for long recordings and shaped marks;
      repeated short marks no longer exclude dash evidence.
    - Preserve regular-file permissions during replacement and reject symlink
      destinations. New replacement paths respect the process umask.
    - Avoid repeated validation and deep copies of internal decoding snapshots.
    - Verify the minimum PDL version and macOS Intel; use Strawberry Perl
      for Windows native builds and retain downloadable timing evidence.
